<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Martin of Aragon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1356">1356</a>–<a href="/years/1410">1410</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Martin the Humane, Martin I of Aragon</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Martin, called the Humane, was king of Aragon from 1396 to 1410 and also king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> from 1409. The last ruler of the house of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcelona">Barcelona</a> in the male line, he lost his only legitimate son, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-i-of-sicily">Martin the Younger</a>, in 1409 and died the next year without naming an undisputed heir. The resulting interregnum ended with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/compromise-of-caspe">Compromise of Caspe</a> in 1412, which gave the throne to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-i-of-aragon">Ferdinand of Antequera</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/martin-of-aragon.jpg" alt="Martin of Aragon" width="320" height="363" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Miniatura_de_Mart%C3%ADn_I_de_Arag%C3%B3n.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
